cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Proof of Human Intent: Cryptographically Verifiable Human Approval for AI-Driven Software Development"
abstract: >-
  Proof of Human Intent (PoHI) is a protocol that creates cryptographically
  verifiable proof that a real human approved critical software actions. It
  combines proof-of-personhood (e.g. World ID zero-knowledge proofs), Git/DID
  signing, and an append-only transparency log (IETF SCITT) to answer who
  approved an action, what was approved, and when.
type: software
